body: 'HONEST LIMITS (Aegis, for the record — the report must restate these): (1) library boundary honest, not enforced (resolveNative importable; enforcement at the two gates; Bash-denial is the procedural answer); (2) a resolves-strand without underGrant is presumed human — library-reaching agents are cryptographically indistinguishable (accepted, TD-136); (3) grant store + key registry are same-OS-user writable — edits detected, self-consistent forgeries not; the runbook write-deny on .warpline/{keys,grants}/** is the load-bearing authority boundary; (4) recordedAt is writer-asserted except server-stamped granted resolves; (5) key re-mint is not revocation — superseded keys verify forever, incl. on new strands (deferred by design); (6) in-box re-key undetectable (no git witness, Q2 ruling); (7) knotClass scope stored but never matches (fail-closed); branch scope effectively selvage-only. Build-D fixture finding: signed-from pins at the selvage tip while an unadmitted scratch proposal can sit later in the ledger — mint keys BEFORE agents propose (runbook ordering). Builder-stop pattern recurred 4/6 agent runs (stops before .purpose/report; resumed via SendMessage each time).'
